---
tracker:
  kind: linear
  endpoint: https://api.linear.app/graphql
  api_key: "$LINEAR_API_KEY"
  project_slug: "@SYMPHONY_LINEAR_PROJECT_SLUG@"
  required_labels: []
  active_states:
    - Todo
    - In Progress
    - Rework
    - Merging
    - Human Review
  terminal_states:
    - Closed
    - Cancelled
    - Canceled
    - Duplicate
    - Done
polling:
  interval_ms: @SYMPHONY_POLL_INTERVAL_MS@
workspace:
  root: "@SYMPHONY_WORKSPACE_ROOT@"
worker:
  provider: cua
  ssh_options:
    - BatchMode=yes
    - StrictHostKeyChecking=no
    - UserKnownHostsFile=/dev/null
    - ConnectTimeout=5
    - LogLevel=ERROR
    - IdentityFile=@SYMPHONY_CUA_SSH_IDENTITY_FILE@
    - IdentitiesOnly=yes
cua:
  driver: docker
  host: "@SYMPHONY_CUA_HOST@"
  image: "@SYMPHONY_CUA_IMAGE@"
  name_prefix: "@SYMPHONY_CUA_NAME_PREFIX@"
  ssh_user: cua
  ssh_authorized_key_path: "@SYMPHONY_CUA_SSH_AUTHORIZED_KEY_PATH@"
  delete_on_terminal: @SYMPHONY_CUA_DELETE_ON_TERMINAL@
  wait_for_ssh: true
  launch_timeout_ms: @SYMPHONY_CUA_LAUNCH_TIMEOUT_MS@
  volumes: []
  docker_args: []
hooks:
  after_create: |
    set -eu
    git clone --depth 1 --branch "@SYMPHONY_SOURCE_REPO_BRANCH@" "@SYMPHONY_SOURCE_REPO_URL@" .
    if [ -n "@SYMPHONY_AFTER_CREATE_EXTRA@" ]; then
      @SYMPHONY_AFTER_CREATE_EXTRA@
    fi
agent:
  max_concurrent_agents: @SYMPHONY_MAX_CONCURRENT_AGENTS@
  max_turns: @SYMPHONY_MAX_TURNS@
codex:
  command: >
    @SYMPHONY_CODEX_COMMAND@
  approval_policy: never
  thread_sandbox: workspace-write
  turn_sandbox_policy: null
observability:
  dashboard_enabled: true
server:
  host: "@SYMPHONY_DASHBOARD_HOST@"
  port: @SYMPHONY_DASHBOARD_PORT@
---

You are working on Linear issue `{{ issue.identifier }}` for the project handled by this Symphony instance.

Symphony is running Codex on the host orchestrator. The issue workspace itself is a CUA sandbox.
When you need to inspect, edit, run commands, or validate project code, use the sandbox tools:

- `sandbox_exec` for headless shell commands in the CUA workspace.
- `sandbox_visible_exec` for commands, app starts, browser sessions, demos, or tests that must be visible through noVNC.
- `sandbox_read_file` for reading files from the CUA workspace.
- `sandbox_write_file` for writing files into the CUA workspace.
- `linear_graphql` for Linear updates and issue context.

Do not use host-local shell commands or host-local file edits for project work unless explicitly instructed by Symphony.

Issue:
- Identifier: {{ issue.identifier }}
- Title: {{ issue.title }}
- State: {{ issue.state }}
- URL: {{ issue.url }}
- Labels: {{ issue.labels }}

Description:
{% if issue.description %}
{{ issue.description }}
{% else %}
No description provided.
{% endif %}

Operating rules:

1. Work autonomously end to end inside the CUA sandbox.
2. Keep a single Linear workpad comment current with plan, acceptance criteria, validation, and final status.
3. Reproduce or inspect the issue before changing code when possible.
4. Run focused validation before marking work complete.
5. Build sanitized, production-scale local data under production-like settings when the task needs realistic product validation.
6. Inventory every user-facing feature, role, route, button, input, modal, state, and workflow affected by the issue.
7. Define documented acceptance criteria and a finite, risk-based edge-case list before broad validation.
8. Test as a real user and log every bug with reproduction evidence.
9. Review findings for shared causes and dependencies; implement coherent fixes with regression tests.
10. Rerun the full affected inventory and stop only at a clean pass or a blocked handoff.
11. Use `sandbox_visible_exec` and the sandbox GUI/noVNC path for UI validation when the task is visual, interactive, demo-oriented, or real-user tested. Record transcript paths from `.symphony/visible-exec/` in the workpad.
12. Ask before production access, sensitive data access, or destructive actions.
13. If blocked by missing project auth, repo auth, secrets, hardware, or external services, document the exact blocker in the workpad and stop.
14. Do not copy host credentials into the sandbox unless the project workflow explicitly requires it.
